<div class="takeaways">
  <p class="takeaways__title">Roof underlayment types in 60 seconds</p>
  <ul>
    <li>There are three families of roof underlayment: asphalt-saturated felt (#15 and #30 roofing paper), synthetic, and self-adhered membranes (rubberized asphalt or peel-and-stick synthetic).</li>
    <li>Synthetic underlayment is now the default under shingles on most Austin re-roofs: lighter, stronger, safer to walk on and far more UV-tolerant than felt.</li>
